# The approach and alighting, in a flying boat: down a three-degree
# glidepath to the water, on to the step, and off it to rest.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# **The technique is the FAA's**, from its Seaplane, Skiplane, and Float/Ski
# Equipped Helicopter Operations Handbook (FAA-H-8083-23), chapter 6, "Normal
# Landing": full flap and a stabilised approach at the approach speed; the
# nose raised to the attitude she taxies on the step at as the water comes up,
# and touching down on the step; the throttles closed once she is definitely
# on the water, and the attitude held until she comes off the step. The
# FlightGear model's notes add "beware of water-loops - keep the nose up".
# The approach speed is `vref`, a third above the stall with everything
# down, which for the Short S.23 is measured from its model (ASSETS.md).
#
# **Alighting is asked of the hull, not of any wheel**: `hydro/active-norm` is
# JSBSim's own word for the hull being in the water.
#
# **The bands are the other classes'**, and are met with room: flown by the
# AI pilot the Short S.23, whose reference speed is 86 knots, holds 85 to 88
# down the approach and 87 over the water, and is on the water with her
# throttles closed.

name Approach and alighting in a flying boat
teaches seaplane

stage The approach
do Join the approach into wind, flaps fully down
do Hold the approach speed and let her come down the glidepath
hold velocities/vc-kts vref-10 vref+15 Hold the approach speed
need velocities/h-dot-fps >= -30 Arrive over the water coming down the glidepath, not falling
until position/h-agl-ft <= 50

stage Over the water
do Hold the approach speed as the water comes up
hold velocities/vc-kts vref-10 vref+15 Cross on to the water on speed
until position/h-agl-ft <= 40

stage Alighting and the run
do Raise the nose to the step attitude and touch down on the step
do Close the throttles once she is on the water, and keep the nose up as she comes off the step
need fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.15 Close the throttles once she is on the water
need hydro/active-norm >= 0.5 Put her down on the water
until velocities/vc-kts <= 20
